### Tested versions

4.4 beta 3

### System information

Windows10 - Godot v4.4 beta3

### Issue description

When calling a method with more than two overloaded versions and a vararg parameter, the correct parameter type cannot be recognized, as demonstrated below:

### Steps to reproduce

```kotlin
class TestClass {
    companion object {
        @JvmStatic
        fun testMethod(int: Int,array: IntArray): String {
            return "IntArray"
        }

        @JvmStatic
        fun testMethod(int: Int,vararg args: String): String {
            return "StringArray"
        }
    }
}
```

When I call this class in Godot, it fails to recognize the parameter types correctly, causing the wrong method to be invoked every time.

```gdscript
func _ready() -> void:
	var javaClass = JavaClassWrapper.wrap("com.godot.game.TestClass")
	print('from kotlin:' + javaClass.testMethod(1,["asd"]))
```

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c4071e5-76ea-4285-8d88-de0cc5751260)
When I pass a parameter of type String, the first method is invoked instead of the second method with the vararg parameter.

